---
import SectionHeader from '../ui/SectionHeader.astro';
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-6 pb-28 md:px-12">
  <SectionHeader eyebrow="Philosophy" headingLight="Why" headingBold="“Liminal”?" />

  <!-- The word on the left, the promise on the right (stacked on phones) -->
  <div data-reveal class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12">
    <!-- The word -->
    <div>
      <p class="mb-4 font-display text-xl leading-[1.5] tracking-[-0.01em] text-title md:text-2xl" style="font-weight: var(--weight-light)">
        <em>Liminal</em> means threshold — the space of crossing from one side to another.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-[1.7] text-body md:text-[17px]">
        Learning a language isn't really about vocabulary or grammar. It's a door. On the other side of that door is a culture, a way of thinking, relationships and experiences you simply cannot access any other way.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The promise -->
    <div>
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted">The journey</p>
      <h3 class="mb-4 font-display text-xl tracking-[-0.02em] text-title md:text-2xl">
        <span style="font-weight: var(--weight-bold)">I did it.</span>
        <span style="font-weight: var(--weight-light)"> We'll do it together.</span>
      </h3>
      <p class="text-base leading-[1.7] text-body md:text-[17px]">
        I made the jump myself — from classroom methods to learning Japanese through immersion, up to JLPT N2 (roughly CEFR B2). I never considered myself a “gifted” learner: what got me there was consistency, not talent. I'm not observing your journey from the outside — I'm on the same road, a few steps ahead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a href="/about/" data-reveal class="mt-8 inline-block text-[15px] font-semibold text-accent">Read my story →</a>
</section>
